# Intentionally minimal.
#
# There is NO catch-all rewrite here. Every legitimate route has a real file in dist:
# 664 prerendered content pages, plus shells for the six app-only routes (tree/settings/
# search in both languages). Anything not matching a file is genuinely missing, and
# Cloudflare Pages serves dist/404.html with a real 404 status for it.
#
# A `/*  /index.html  200` fallback would answer HTTP 200 for every bad URL — a "soft
# 404", which search engines treat as a quality signal against the site. Do not add one
# back without also removing 404.html.

# The bare root carries no language. It still goes to French -- the lead market, and a
# real page for a crawler rather than a JS-dependent blank -- but it carries `l=auto`,
# which tells the app this visitor did NOT ask for French: they asked for nothing.
#
# That distinction is the whole point. Cloudflare Pages cannot branch a redirect on
# Accept-Language, so the language choice has to happen in the app; without a marker the
# app cannot tell a root visitor from someone opening a /fr link that a French speaker
# sent them, and correcting the second would be worse than not correcting the first.
# The app strips the parameter as it goes, so nothing downstream ever sees it.
/    /fr?l=auto    302

